From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] update_engine: scaled DLCs from NickelOS's update server

Scaled DLCs (116 on NickelOS: handwriting, text-to-speech voices, extra
fonts, ...) were downloaded from Google's CDN under the image's builder
path. Google has none for NickelOS builds, so every install failed
(kScaledInstallationError), and NickelOS asks Google for nothing by
default. They now come from update.nickelos.dev/dlc, under the builder path
nickel-build-stock sets (nickel-release/R<milestone>-<version>).
---
--- a/update_engine/cros/install_action.cc	2026-10-12 10:48:44.944109016 -0400
+++ b/update_engine/cros/install_action.cc	2026-10-12 10:48:44.946128879 -0400
@@ -31,11 +31,16 @@
 namespace chromeos_update_engine {
 
 namespace {
-constexpr char kBandaidUrl[] = "https://edgedl.me.gvt1.com/edgedl/dlc";
-constexpr char kLorryUrl[] = "https://dl.google.com/dlc";
+// NickelOS: scaled DLCs (handwriting, voices, fonts, ...) come from
+// NickelOS's update server, not Google's: Google has no NickelOS builds, and
+// NickelOS asks Google for nothing by default. The path below them is the
+// image's builder path (nickel-release/R<milestone>-<version>, set by
+// nickel-build-stock), where push-dlc puts each build's DLC images.
+constexpr char kBandaidUrl[] = "https://update.nickelos.dev/dlc";
+constexpr char kLorryUrl[] = "https://update.nickelos.dev/dlc";
 
-constexpr char kBandaidArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://edgedl.me.gvt1.com/edgedl";
-constexpr char kLorryArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://dl.google.com";
+constexpr char kBandaidArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://update.nickelos.dev";
+constexpr char kLorryArtifactsMetaUrl[] = "https://update.nickelos.dev";
 
 constexpr char kUrlNameBandaid[] = "<BANDAID>";
 constexpr char kUrlNameLorry[] = "<LORRY>";
